POST /assurance/validators
	corpus: command
	example {"name":"manifest","pattern":"^MANIFEST-\\d{8}T\\d{6}Z\\.txt$","backup_set_id":"api-server/var-backups","script":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nexit 0\n"}: command
	example {"name":"dumps","pattern":"\\.sql\\.gz$","script":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nexit 0\n"}: command
	example {"name":"dumps","pattern":"\\.sql\\.gz$","env":"workflow","script":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nexit 0\n"}: command
	body that isn't JSON: malformed: there is no verb that uploads a validator from a request body

POST /auth/enroll
	no command: the first administrator is made by `retnd-web auth create-admin --username U --password-stdin`, offline, against the store, and it refuses while a server holds the store or once an administrator exists; there is no routed verb for it, because there is no engine account to sign in as yet

POST /auth/forgot-password
	no command: there is no verb that asks for a password-reset email from a terminal; it is the browser's path for an account with a working mail server, and a terminal that can reach the engine at all can change the password with `retnd auth password`

POST /auth/login
	no command: a login opens a browser session, and a terminal holds no session: a routed command signs in with $RETND_API_USERNAME and $RETND_API_PASSWORD for the one invocation, so there is nothing to type

POST /auth/logout
	no command: a logout ends a browser session, and a terminal holds none

POST /auth/password
	corpus: command
	example: command
	body that isn't JSON: command

POST /auth/recovery/test
	example: command
	body that isn't JSON: command

POST /auth/reset-password
	no command: there is no verb that redeems a password-reset token from a terminal. An administrator locked out with no mail configured does have a way back in: `retnd-web auth set-password --username U --password-stdin`, offline, with the server stopped

POST /auth/verify-email
	corpus: command
